% SCAFFOLDING stand-in for SIMPOS's class
% `essential_scrolling_menu_with_superior_input_buffer`, compiled by
% psi/espc.py into the package `simpos`.  It is NOT SIMPOS: the class is
% lost (docs/simpos/subsystems/window.md §0.3, §1.6, the scrolling menus).
% MENDELS (IFS No.61), 2026-11-27: its port window and the natures of its
% tsl_menu and parts_normal_window (mendel_win.esp create_port_window/6,
% create_menu/7; win_class.esp:5-10, 50-61), the scrolling lists inside
% its `base`; disc's structure candidate menus (disp_win.esp:322, 374);
% kappa2 wsmenu.esp:36; three held application classes as a nature
% (window.md §1.3).
%
% THE NATURE LIST IS INFERENCE: no composite's list is printed (window.md
% §1.6).  From the name (scrolling -> as_scrolling_menu, essential_ the
% composite without the extras, _with_superior_input_buffer that mixin),
% TM-125 p8-12 (every menu inherits as_menu; a single-select menu takes
% mouse input), and the held scrolling menus' own lists (video
% fdd_utility_file_menu: labeled_sash, as_scrolling_menu,
% as_multiple_select, as_mouse_input, temporary_window, window.md §1.5;
% MENDELS temporary_turn_menu and inferior_turn_menu, win_class.esp:27-35,
% 107-116: labeled_sash, [with_superior_input_buffer,] as_scrolling_menu,
% as_single_select, as_mouse_input, ...).  labeled_sash: MENDELS gives its
% port window set_label_flag(off) and disc sets a title (disp_win.esp:
% 323), so it has a label by default (INFERENCE).  as_menu
% comes with as_scrolling_menu (as_scrolling_menu.esp, which does not
% scroll); as_single_select and as_mouse_input are not stood in:
% as_menu.esp draws one column and takes a left click (basic_window.esp);
% a send that only they would answer is refused loudly.  It has no method
% of its own.

class essential_scrolling_menu_with_superior_input_buffer has

nature
        labeled_sash,
        with_superior_input_buffer,
        as_scrolling_menu,
        as_single_select,
        as_mouse_input,
        inferior_window;

end.
